  <Page id="8">
    <Text>You pretend to trip and grab Aladdin's robes to keep from falling. Surprised, he puts out his arms to hold you up; quick as lightning you take his hand and slide the ring off: a master stroke. You apologise and take your leave.

Pleased with yourself, you examine the haul: the sapphire in the ring pulses with energy and an Efreet comes out of it, a magical spirit.

— Who disturbs me? What can I do for you? —

— Can you carry me to Ali Baba? —

— You are too heavy; I can only carry small objects —</Text>
